# PROJECT: ONLINE BOOK STORE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

## 1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack Java developer, software architect, database designer, UI/UX designer, security engineer, and software tester.

Develop a complete, functional, responsive web application called "Online Book Store Management System."

This is an academic micro-project for a B.Tech Computer Science Engineering student at Alliance University.

The application must be suitable for a university project demonstration, technical review, and viva examination.

IMPORTANT:
Do not create only a frontend prototype, static website, UI mockup, or collection of nonfunctional buttons.

Build a complete working application with:

* Responsive frontend.
* Java backend.
* MySQL database.
* Java database connectivity through JDBC.
* User registration and authentication.
* Customer and administrator roles.
* Book catalogue and search.
* Shopping cart.
* Order placement and management.
* Inventory management.
* Input validation.
* Error handling.
* Testing.
* Setup instructions and project documentation.

Every visible button, link, form, filter, menu, and action must have a meaningful, implemented behavior.

Do not claim that a feature works unless it is implemented and tested.

If an external service requires credentials, clearly document the requirement and provide an appropriate local development alternative without pretending that the external integration is active.

