## 31. FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

Consider the project complete only when the following conditions have been addressed and tested:

[ ] The application builds successfully.

[ ] The database schema can be created from the supplied SQL files.

[ ] Sample book data can be loaded.

[ ] The homepage displays books from the database.

[ ] Search works correctly.

[ ] Filters and sorting work correctly.

[ ] Customer registration works.

[ ] Duplicate email registration is rejected.

[ ] Login and logout work.

[ ] Passwords are not stored in plain text.

[ ] Customers cannot access administrator functions.

[ ] Customers cannot access other customers' orders.

[ ] Administrators can add books.

[ ] Administrators can edit books.

[ ] Administrators can deactivate or safely remove books.

[ ] Administrators can manage categories.

[ ] The shopping cart works.

[ ] Cart totals are calculated on the server.

[ ] Checkout validates current stock.

[ ] Orders are stored in MySQL.

[ ] Order items are stored correctly.

[ ] Stock updates are transaction-safe.

[ ] Failed orders do not leave partial database changes.

[ ] Order history displays the correct customer's orders.

[ ] Order status updates follow business rules.

[ ] Inventory reports work.

[ ] Sales reports use actual database records.

[ ] Every displayed button has an implemented action.

[ ] Forms display meaningful validation errors.

[ ] The interface works on mobile and desktop.

[ ] Automated tests have been run and their results documented.

[ ] Setup instructions work for the generated project.

[ ] The final project report and viva documentation are included.

